1
00:00:00,366 --> 00:00:01,533
Have you ever noticed

2
00:00:01,933 --> 00:00:04,166
the thing that stings most about ordering takeout now

3
00:00:04,233 --> 00:00:05,966
isn't that one dish is super expensive

4
00:00:05,966 --> 00:00:08,366
it's that you just wanted a quick bite

5
00:00:08,566 --> 00:00:11,066
but the checkout page seems to remind you

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,266
this little meal of yours

7
00:00:12,366 --> 00:00:14,066
somehow isn't so casual anymore

8
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,000
Delivery fee

9
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:15,766
packaging fee

10
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:16,533
service fee

11
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:17,766
spend-more-save-more bundles

12
00:00:17,766 --> 00:00:18,766
member coupons

13
00:00:18,966 --> 00:00:20,166
you tap around and around

14
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,833
and it still ends up pricier than you expected

15
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,633
Most people's first reaction is

16
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,433
did the restaurants turn greedy

17
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:27,233
is the platform fleecing us again

18
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,833
Of course there are complex pricing rules behind this

19
00:00:30,033 --> 00:00:33,566
but this video wants to make a more down-to-earth point

20
00:00:33,733 --> 00:00:35,033
Takeout keeps getting more expensive

21
00:00:35,133 --> 00:00:37,333
not just because a bowl of rice costs more

22
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:40,233
but because what you buy stopped being just a bowl of rice long ago

23
00:00:40,366 --> 00:00:41,933
You're buying not having to go out

24
00:00:41,966 --> 00:00:43,000
not having to wait in line

25
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,000
not having to wash dishes

26
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:45,333
not having to talk to anyone

27
00:00:45,366 --> 00:00:47,666
not having to make another decision when you're tired

28
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:51,200
What takeout really sells is taking the hassle off your hands

29
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:52,333
The pricier the hassle

30
00:00:52,366 --> 00:00:53,566
the pricier the takeout

31
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,066
Seven thirty in the evening

32
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:56,600
you just got off work

33
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:58,266
your brain still a bit numb

34
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,766
you don't want to change clothes

35
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,133
you don't want to scrub a pot

36
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,000
there's actually a restaurant downstairs

37
00:01:03,233 --> 00:01:04,766
just ten minutes on foot

38
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,866
but you still open the takeout app

39
00:01:07,166 --> 00:01:08,200
because in this moment

40
00:01:08,366 --> 00:01:09,800
what you lack isn't a restaurant

41
00:01:09,933 --> 00:01:11,266
what you lack is not having to move

42
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,766
This is the truest value of takeout

43
00:01:13,966 --> 00:01:16,066
it doesn't just bring food to you

44
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,966
it handles a whole string of small hassles for you

45
00:01:19,133 --> 00:01:19,900
Going out

46
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:20,566
waiting for a seat

47
00:01:20,566 --> 00:01:21,233
ordering

48
00:01:21,233 --> 00:01:21,900
paying

49
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:22,633
walking back

50
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:23,666
cleaning up the dishes

51
00:01:23,766 --> 00:01:25,633
Each of these alone is no big deal

52
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:27,033
but when you're worn out after a long day

53
00:01:27,166 --> 00:01:29,066
each one feels like it's charging you

54
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,400
Takeout bundles all these charges together

55
00:01:31,433 --> 00:01:32,600
into a single button

56
00:01:32,733 --> 00:01:33,533
you tap once

57
00:01:33,566 --> 00:01:34,800
and half the hassle disappears

58
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:36,766
So a lot of people complain takeout is expensive

59
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,533
but order it again next time

60
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:40,133
not because you're irrational

61
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,033
but because you know perfectly well

62
00:01:42,166 --> 00:01:43,833
tonight's ten-something yuan difference

63
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:45,166
buys you a breather

64
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:46,533
you don't have to go downstairs again

65
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,166
don't have to make small talk with the owner

66
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:49,466
don't have to wait in the shop

67
00:01:49,566 --> 00:01:51,333
don't have to carry a takeout box back

68
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,066
This ease is very real

69
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:55,566
it's just that you never saw it as its own thing before

70
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:57,066
Takeout put a price tag on it

71
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,533
and only then do you suddenly realize

72
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,466
convenience itself costs this much

73
00:02:00,633 --> 00:02:02,400
The cost people overlook most easily

74
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,633
is all the little things you don't want to do yourself

75
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:06,600
There's another cost that's even more hidden

76
00:02:06,633 --> 00:02:07,933
it's called decision cost

77
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,933
You think ordering takeout saves effort

78
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:12,733
but sometimes you scroll the app for twenty minutes

79
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:14,400
this one's minimum order is too high

80
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,833
that one's delivery is too slow

81
00:02:15,966 --> 00:02:17,266
this one's reviews are so-so

82
00:02:17,366 --> 00:02:19,166
that one's photos look pretty good

83
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,800
in the end the more you pick the more annoyed you get

84
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:22,133
you even lose your appetite from waiting

85
00:02:22,366 --> 00:02:24,566
Here takeout runs into a paradox

86
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:26,666
it was meant to save you from deciding

87
00:02:26,766 --> 00:02:28,133
but with too many choices

88
00:02:28,166 --> 00:02:29,933
it creates a new kind of drain

89
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,166
Modern people's tiredness

90
00:02:31,166 --> 00:02:32,633
often isn't physical tiredness

91
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,066
it's too-many-choices tiredness

92
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:34,966
What to eat

93
00:02:34,966 --> 00:02:35,800
which place to order from

94
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:37,066
whether to hit the discount threshold

95
00:02:37,166 --> 00:02:39,033
whether to switch to a cheaper one

96
00:02:39,133 --> 00:02:40,400
you just want to eat

97
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:42,533
but you're forced into a string of small decisions

98
00:02:42,766 --> 00:02:44,400
So what's truly expensive about takeout

99
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,533
sometimes isn't the number on the checkout page

100
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:49,000
it's that you hand over the last bit of attention in your day

101
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,466
to a menu too

102
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,033
If you often feel tired even after ordering takeout

103
00:02:53,133 --> 00:02:54,266
you're not being precious

104
00:02:54,366 --> 00:02:56,000
it's that even eating

105
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,166
hasn't been freed from choice for you

106
00:02:58,533 --> 00:03:00,466
What makes takeout addictive

107
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:02,033
isn't just the convenience

108
00:03:02,433 --> 00:03:04,866
it's that it turns price into a game

109
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:06,566
spend thirty save eight

110
00:03:06,733 --> 00:03:08,000
a coupon takes off three more

111
00:03:08,233 --> 00:03:09,633
grab another member voucher

112
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:11,800
add a side dish to just hit the threshold

113
00:03:12,033 --> 00:03:13,366
it looks like you came out ahead

114
00:03:13,533 --> 00:03:14,633
but after you order

115
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,566
you may have just gone from one meal

116
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,866
to one meal plus a snack you didn't even want

117
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,666
The price didn't disappear

118
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,733
it just showed up somewhere else

119
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,466
This is why so many find takeout expensive yet can't quit it

120
00:03:27,766 --> 00:03:30,200
Takeout apps rarely tell you straight

121
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:32,000
whether this meal is actually worth it

122
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:34,766
it's more like it keeps handing you a task

123
00:03:34,966 --> 00:03:35,933
add a little more

124
00:03:35,933 --> 00:03:36,933
grab one more voucher

125
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
switch to another place

126
00:03:38,133 --> 00:03:39,333
wait three more minutes

127
00:03:39,533 --> 00:03:41,166
you just wanted to eat

128
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:43,033
but you end up solving a puzzle

129
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,233
Sometimes to save five yuan

130
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,733
you spend ten more minutes

131
00:03:46,933 --> 00:03:48,400
order an extra snack

132
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,166
and make yourself even hungrier

133
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:52,333
You think you're being shrewd

134
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:54,566
but the platform has shifted your attention

135
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,400
from the total to the discount

136
00:03:56,566 --> 00:03:57,566
That's clever

137
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:59,566
because people are sensitive to cheap

138
00:03:59,966 --> 00:04:01,600
but numb to total cost

139
00:04:01,766 --> 00:04:03,266
Total cost isn't just money

140
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,466
it's also time

141
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,400
attention

142
00:04:05,433 --> 00:04:06,666
the impatience of waiting

143
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:09,633
and that little emptiness staring at the plastic box afterward

144
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,533
You may have saved three yuan

145
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:13,733
but paid twenty minutes of agonizing

146
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,600
Few people ever do this math

147
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,366
What takeout does best

148
00:04:17,433 --> 00:04:19,400
isn't making you feel it's absolutely cheap

149
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,966
it's making you feel you're getting a deal

150
00:04:22,233 --> 00:04:23,600
The feeling of scoring a deal

151
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,266
makes people let their guard down

152
00:04:25,433 --> 00:04:27,333
There's another very common move

153
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:28,400
to hit the discount threshold

154
00:04:28,533 --> 00:04:30,133
you add a drink

155
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,433
to get free delivery

156
00:04:31,566 --> 00:04:33,000
you add a side

157
00:04:33,166 --> 00:04:34,266
to use a coupon

158
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:36,133
you switch from the place you wanted

159
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,566
to another place you didn't really want

160
00:04:38,766 --> 00:04:40,633
In the end you look like you saved money

161
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:42,366
but after eating you find

162
00:04:42,533 --> 00:04:44,733
an unfinished bottle on the table

163
00:04:44,833 --> 00:04:47,233
an unneeded load in your stomach

164
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:49,533
and a few extra boxes in the trash

165
00:04:49,766 --> 00:04:51,933
This is the slyest thing about discounts

166
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:54,466
they make you think you're cutting losses

167
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:56,866
when you may be buying excess

168
00:04:57,133 --> 00:04:59,466
If cheap makes you buy what you don't need

169
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:00,833
it isn't cheap

170
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:03,166
it's just waste under another name

171
00:05:03,566 --> 00:05:04,666
Looking further

172
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:06,966
why does takeout keep getting more expensive

173
00:05:06,966 --> 00:05:10,000
because it eats up what modern people have least of

174
00:05:10,033 --> 00:05:10,833
time

175
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:11,533
energy

176
00:05:11,533 --> 00:05:12,200
patience

177
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,166
You don't want to go downstairs

178
00:05:13,166 --> 00:05:14,233
someone has to go downstairs

179
00:05:14,233 --> 00:05:15,133
you don't want to wait in line

180
00:05:15,133 --> 00:05:16,200
someone has to wait for the food

181
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,133
you don't want to brave the rain

182
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:18,800
someone has to ride out in a raincoat

183
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,166
you don't want to deal with people

184
00:05:20,166 --> 00:05:22,566
the system and rider handle the communication for you

185
00:05:22,566 --> 00:05:23,800
The hassle you save

186
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,133
doesn't vanish into thin air

187
00:05:25,133 --> 00:05:27,100
it just shifts onto someone else

188
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:28,633
So takeout isn't magic

189
00:05:28,633 --> 00:05:30,400
it's a very long relay

190
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,500
the restaurant preps the food

191
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,566
the platform assigns the order

192
00:05:32,566 --> 00:05:33,533
the rider picks it up

193
00:05:33,533 --> 00:05:34,433
delivers it on the road

194
00:05:34,433 --> 00:05:35,366
confirms at your door

195
00:05:35,366 --> 00:05:36,500
by the time it's in your hands

196
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,933
all you see is a bag

197
00:05:37,933 --> 00:05:39,966
but behind the bag is a whole operation

198
00:05:39,966 --> 00:05:41,300
The faster this operation runs

199
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,166
the more on time

200
00:05:42,166 --> 00:05:44,400
the better it satisfies your urge to eat anytime

201
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,800
the higher its cost

202
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,533
You want it delivered in twenty minutes

203
00:05:47,533 --> 00:05:48,833
want the food still hot

204
00:05:48,833 --> 00:05:50,133
want the soup not to spill

205
00:05:50,133 --> 00:05:51,600
want the rider to come upstairs

206
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,266
want support to fix any problem

207
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:55,166
Each of these expectations is reasonable

208
00:05:55,166 --> 00:05:56,833
but reasonable doesn't mean free

209
00:05:56,833 --> 00:05:58,333
Modern life is strange

210
00:05:58,333 --> 00:05:59,966
we complain about high prices

211
00:05:59,966 --> 00:06:02,333
while wanting the world to respond to us instantly

212
00:06:02,333 --> 00:06:03,300
order and it must arrive

213
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,300
ask and it must reply

214
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,633
get tired and someone must catch you

215
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:07,100
This immediacy itself

216
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,100
is a very expensive way of living

217
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:11,233
So what stings about takeout prices

218
00:06:11,233 --> 00:06:12,700
isn't just that one meal went up

219
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,000
it's that it lets you see

220
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,166
that my time my laziness my dread of hassle

221
00:06:16,166 --> 00:06:17,733
have all been openly priced

222
00:06:17,733 --> 00:06:20,833
That's why takeout looks more and more like a living bill

223
00:06:20,833 --> 00:06:22,133
it doesn't happen once in a while

224
00:06:22,133 --> 00:06:23,400
it happens every day

225
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,233
no time for breakfast

226
00:06:24,233 --> 00:06:24,600
order

227
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,766
don't want to walk for lunch

228
00:06:25,766 --> 00:06:26,166
order

229
00:06:26,166 --> 00:06:27,166
too tired for dinner

230
00:06:27,166 --> 00:06:27,433
order

231
00:06:27,433 --> 00:06:28,766
want a late-night bite

232
00:06:28,766 --> 00:06:29,300
order again

233
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:30,600
One meal looks like little

234
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:32,000
but stacked over a day it adds up

235
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,333
look back over a month

236
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:35,833
and you'll find you didn't spend it on any one meal

237
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:38,433
but on a life that's gone unplanned for a long time

238
00:06:38,433 --> 00:06:40,100
The most stinging thing about takeout

239
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,533
is that it keeps a record for you

240
00:06:41,533 --> 00:06:43,766
of how often you were too tired to care for yourself

241
00:06:43,766 --> 00:06:44,633
and how often

242
00:06:44,633 --> 00:06:46,166
you handed life's temporary mess

243
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:48,433
to a rider and a plastic bag

244
00:06:48,833 --> 00:06:51,400
So how can ordinary people order takeout more clear-headed

245
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,166
First

246
00:06:52,233 --> 00:06:53,433
don't just look at the dish price

247
00:06:53,533 --> 00:06:54,333
look at the total

248
00:06:54,333 --> 00:06:55,033
delivery fee

249
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:55,766
packaging fee

250
00:06:55,766 --> 00:06:56,600
add-on cost

251
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,533
plus the time you spend picking a place

252
00:06:58,533 --> 00:06:59,500
count it all in

253
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,833
If a meal goes from twenty to thirty-five

254
00:07:01,833 --> 00:07:03,233
you should know what the extra money

255
00:07:03,233 --> 00:07:04,766
is buying in convenience

256
00:07:04,766 --> 00:07:05,500
Second

257
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,033
sort takeout into two kinds

258
00:07:07,033 --> 00:07:08,133
one is for emergencies

259
00:07:08,133 --> 00:07:09,200
one is out of habit

260
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,033
working too late

261
00:07:10,033 --> 00:07:11,000
feeling unwell

262
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:11,966
terrible weather

263
00:07:11,966 --> 00:07:13,433
in these moments takeout helps you

264
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,166
but if every day it's just not wanting to think

265
00:07:15,166 --> 00:07:15,800
not wanting to move

266
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:16,766
not wanting to plan

267
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:19,466
then takeout turns from a tool into a fixed expense

268
00:07:19,566 --> 00:07:20,600
A tool used now and then

269
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,700
you'll be grateful for

270
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,200
a fixed expense charged daily

271
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,433
will drag you down

272
00:07:24,433 --> 00:07:25,166
Third

273
00:07:25,166 --> 00:07:27,500
prepare a few no-thinking meals for yourself

274
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,833
something frozen in the fridge

275
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:30,033
a few eggs at home

276
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:31,666
a regular little shop downstairs

277
00:07:31,733 --> 00:07:33,966
a no-fuss set meal near the office

278
00:07:34,033 --> 00:07:36,000
These preparations look ordinary

279
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,833
but they cut down how often when you're most tired

280
00:07:37,833 --> 00:07:39,133
you get pushed along by the platform

281
00:07:39,133 --> 00:07:39,900
The more tired you are

282
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:41,733
the more you need to plan a little ahead

283
00:07:41,733 --> 00:07:43,300
not to become super disciplined

284
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:45,933
but to be charged less by last-minute choices

285
00:07:45,933 --> 00:07:46,600
Fourth

286
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,533
set a budget boundary for takeout

287
00:07:48,533 --> 00:07:49,933
not to punish yourself

288
00:07:49,933 --> 00:07:51,433
but to see the habit

289
00:07:51,433 --> 00:07:53,433
like at most a few times a week

290
00:07:53,433 --> 00:07:55,366
like don't order above a certain amount

291
00:07:55,366 --> 00:07:57,400
like prep two meals ahead on the weekend

292
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,500
You don't have to suddenly become a cook

293
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,300
just turn takeout from the default option

294
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,600
into an active choice

295
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,800
This step is key

296
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,633
because defaults swallow money most easily

297
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,500
You didn't decide to order takeout

298
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:09,066
you just didn't decide not to

299
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:10,166
Many living costs

300
00:08:10,166 --> 00:08:11,833
grow quietly just like this

301
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:13,100
Here's one more little trick

302
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,733
before ordering ask yourself

303
00:08:14,733 --> 00:08:16,533
do I really want this place right now

304
00:08:16,533 --> 00:08:18,666
or do I just want to escape cooking and choosing

305
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:19,833
If the answer is the former

306
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:20,566
then order

307
00:08:20,566 --> 00:08:22,533
and enjoy this convenience with a clear mind

308
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:23,766
If the answer is the latter

309
00:08:23,766 --> 00:08:25,966
you can give yourself a cheaper alternative

310
00:08:25,966 --> 00:08:27,500
like the regular set meal downstairs

311
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,033
like simply boiling noodles at home

312
00:08:29,033 --> 00:08:31,000
like frozen dumplings you stocked ahead

313
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,433
These choices aren't fancy

314
00:08:32,433 --> 00:08:34,966
but they pull you out of momentary exhaustion

315
00:08:34,966 --> 00:08:36,133
A lot of money in life

316
00:08:36,133 --> 00:08:37,533
isn't spent on what you love

317
00:08:37,533 --> 00:08:38,833
it's spent on running out of time

318
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:39,700
no time to think

319
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:40,733
no time to prepare

320
00:08:40,733 --> 00:08:41,966
no time to care for yourself

321
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,766
So every bit you prepare ahead

322
00:08:43,766 --> 00:08:45,966
is really cutting the price for your future self

323
00:08:45,966 --> 00:08:47,133
This isn't anti-consumption

324
00:08:47,133 --> 00:08:49,533
it's taking back the choice from the platform

325
00:08:49,533 --> 00:08:50,900
Ordering takeout one less time

326
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:52,300
won't necessarily save your life

327
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:54,533
but it gives you one more chance to see yourself

328
00:08:54,533 --> 00:08:55,800
Takeout isn't a bad thing

329
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:57,833
it just turned convenience into a product

330
00:08:57,833 --> 00:08:59,166
You can buy convenience

331
00:08:59,166 --> 00:09:01,000
but it's best to know what you're buying

332
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,133
don't hand over every bout of exhaustion

333
00:09:02,133 --> 00:09:03,900
to a checkout page to handle

334
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,300
A truly clear-headed life

335
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:06,833
isn't always cooking for yourself

336
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,966
it's knowing when to buy convenience

337
00:09:08,966 --> 00:09:11,533
and when to take convenience back from habit

338
00:09:11,533 --> 00:09:14,366
Next time we'll talk about the braille on ATMs

339
00:09:14,366 --> 00:09:16,300
a design that many people never use

340
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,566
why does it still exist

341
00:09:17,566 --> 00:09:19,433
because what truly makes a society advanced

342
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:21,500
isn't just how fast it serves the majority

343
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:23,633
but whether it leaves a door open for the few

344
00:09:23,633 --> 00:09:24,600
See you next time
